# Mod projects MP6 receipt: the authoring loop. A project passes (so it has a
# last-good build and a snapshot of its text files). Files are then edited from
# outside the app, which is what copy-file and write-file stand for: an agent or
# a person writing the folder. The first edit imports net without a grant: the
# reload is refused by name, the row shows the diff since the last pass, and
# Roll back puts last-good.wasm back and reloads through the pin. The second
# edit is a component whose turn traps: the turn detaches the mod and keeps the
# trap, Roll back restores the component (the sources stay as edited), and the
# mod attaches and runs a turn again. The host calls no model and holds no key.
# Each frame scrolls the settings pane to the Mod projects row.
# Offline; FRESH profile (TURNSTONE_ROOT, the data root). TURNSTONE_MOD_FIXTURES
# names tests/fixtures/mod-projects (starter/ and alt/, read only).
settle 30
key escape

mod-create ${TURNSTONE_MOD_FIXTURES}/starter
assert event mod-create notes-mod ok
mod-check notes-mod
assert event mod-check notes-mod ok
mod-attach notes-mod
assert event mod-attach notes-mod ok
mod-fixtures notes-mod
assert event mod-fixtures notes-mod ok: 1 of 1 fixtures passed
mod-turn notes-mod set One
assert event mod-turn notes-mod ok: turn set: applied, rev 1
act id:pane:settings
scroll 760 400 -3000
scroll 760 400 700
settle 10
capture 01_passing_build_keeps_last_good

# Edit from outside: the component now imports net, mod.toml declares network
# (no grant), and an agent leaves a note file in src/.
copy-file ${TURNSTONE_MOD_FIXTURES}/alt/net.wasm ${TURNSTONE_ROOT}/mod-projects/notes-mod/component.wasm
write-file ${TURNSTONE_ROOT}/mod-projects/notes-mod/mod.toml mod_id = "notes-mod"\ndisplay_name = "Notes mod"\nversion = "0.1.0"\ncomponent = "component.wasm"\ndocument = "document.txt"\ncapabilities = ["network"]\n
write-file ${TURNSTONE_ROOT}/mod-projects/notes-mod/src/agent_notes.rs // agent: fetch the headline over net\n
mod-reload notes-mod
assert event mod-reload notes-mod refused
assert omnibar open
assert snap suggestions ~ import mere:script/net is not granted
settle 10
capture 02_failing_import_refused_by_name
key escape
scroll 760 400 -3000
scroll 760 400 700
settle 10
capture 03_diff_since_the_last_pass

# Roll back: last-good.wasm over component.wasm, reloaded through the pin on the
# same document. The edited files stay, and the diff still shows them.
mod-rollback notes-mod
assert event mod-rollback notes-mod ok: restored last-good.wasm; reloaded on the same document
mod-turn notes-mod set Two
assert event mod-turn notes-mod ok: turn set: applied, rev 2
scroll 760 400 -3000
scroll 760 400 700
settle 10
capture 04_rolled_back_and_running_again

# Second outside edit: a component that loads but traps on its first turn.
copy-file ${TURNSTONE_MOD_FIXTURES}/alt/trap_turn.wasm ${TURNSTONE_ROOT}/mod-projects/notes-mod/component.wasm
mod-reload notes-mod
assert event mod-reload notes-mod ok: reloaded on the same document
mod-turn notes-mod set Three
assert event mod-turn notes-mod refused
scroll 760 400 -3000
scroll 760 400 700
settle 10
capture 05_trapped_turn_detached_and_kept
scroll 760 400 -3000
scroll 760 400 450
settle 10
capture 05b_trap_kept_and_not_attached

mod-rollback notes-mod
assert event mod-rollback notes-mod ok: restored last-good.wasm; re-admitted; nothing attached
mod-attach notes-mod
assert event mod-attach notes-mod ok
mod-turn notes-mod set Four
assert event mod-turn notes-mod ok: turn set: applied, rev 1
scroll 760 400 -3000
scroll 760 400 700
settle 10
capture 06_rolled_back_attached_and_run_again
scroll 760 400 -3000
scroll 760 400 450
settle 10
capture 06b_status_attached_trap_still_kept
scroll 760 400 -3000
scroll 760 400 1300
settle 10
capture 07_roll_back_button_in_the_actions

log mod projects MP6 receipt complete
